From c402e4809965b7419db07bba7e2284f4c9d3376c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SWG Local Dev <swg-local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:48:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Sandbox Hoth: ordinary creatures, lairs and a world spawner
 (Bellum Gero, AGPL-3.0)

Port of Bellum Gero's (github.com/Miphstoe/BellumGero-Live, 1f4438a1) Hoth mobiles,
lairs and hoth_world spawn group, by outputs/tools/hoth/hoth_port_mobiles.py:
- mobile/hoth: 19 templates with Bellum's stats and levels (owner: keep the endgame
  levels). Loot groups this server lacks are removed; each file names its source,
  licence and changes. The glacial rancor is left out (its body is in no archive the
  client loads).
- 11 lairs (creature_dynamic, creature_lair, npc_dynamic) and spawn/hoth/hoth_world.lua.
- hoth_regions.lua: a world-spawner region (SPAWNAREA + WORLDSPAWNAREA, 1024 at most);
  the outpost's no-spawn circle is unchanged. Only loaded where ZonesEnabled has hoth.

Test galaxy, 14 Oct: clean boot ("hoth Loaded 7 total regions"). A bot probe
(tools/hoth/hoth_creature_probe.py) saw 5 Hoth tauntauns, 8 ice mynocks and a greater
ice mynock 250-360 m south of the pad; the level-1 bot was killed by them.

Agent: Claude
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
